Stop failing the cutover on an error this host logs no matter what.

Applied on top of cutover-wrapper-dialplan-gate.patch.

With the dialplan gate fixed the cutover finished the switch, passed every
live verification, and failed on `service_logged_error_after_cutover`. That
gate asks whether the coordinator, nginx or Asterisk logged anything at error
priority during the cutover window. What they logged was this, four times:

  asterisk: radcli: rc_read_config: can't open
  /etc/radiusclient-ng/radiusclient.conf: No such file or directory

Asterisk on this host loads a RADIUS module whose client configuration was
never installed, and it says so at error level on every single start.

The journal proves it is unrelated to the cutover rather than merely looking
unrelated. Two Asterisk starts happened inside that window: 04:42:13 with the
cutover configuration in place, and 04:42:23 with the original configuration
restored by the rollback. Both logged the identical lines. A message that
survives its own rollback is a property of the installation, not evidence
that the switch broke something -- and since the gate runs after every start,
it could never pass here.

Excluding that one file name is the narrowest correction available: any other
error from any of the three services, including any other radcli error, still
fails the cutover closed. Under `set -o pipefail` the filtered case stays
closed too -- when nothing survives the filter the pipeline exits non-zero and
the gate simply does not fire.

The alternative was making the assumption true instead of the check: install
the missing radiusclient.conf, or noload the RADIUS modules. Both change live
PBX configuration outside the reviewed wrapper, which is exactly what the
wrapper exists to prevent, and neither is required for a working call path.

  before: d287b837b85c3b595d265908fa0cd56b422a1df4f92339373949df3bb1fea1c0
  after:  a57672374a640ce3f3efb8164f1b0085c81afb6706e6a704001a56ee84176a47

--- a/fanum-pbx-coordinator-deploy
+++ b/fanum-pbx-coordinator-deploy
@@ -3302,7 +3302,8 @@
 if journalctl -u fanum-pbx-coordinator.service -u nginx.service -u asterisk.service \
-  --since "$journal_since" --priority=err --no-pager --quiet | grep -q .; then
+  --since "$journal_since" --priority=err --no-pager --quiet \
+  | grep -Fv 'radiusclient-ng/radiusclient.conf' | grep -q .; then
   fail "service_logged_error_after_cutover"
 fi
